+      <!-- ── 1 ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
+      <article class="pj-card" id="linux-automation" data-level="beginner">
+        <div class="pj-head">
+          <div class="pj-num">01</div>
+          <div>
+            <h2>Linux Server Health &amp; Backup Automation</h2>
+            <p>Write Bash scripts that check disk, memory and service health, rotate logs and back up a directory on a schedule.</p>
+            <div class="pj-meta">
+              <span class="pj-pill lvl-beginner">Beginner</span>
+              <span class="pj-pill">~1 weekend</span>
+              <span class="pj-pill">Bash</span><span class="pj-pill">cron</span><span class="pj-pill">systemd</span><span class="pj-pill">SSH</span>
+            </div>
+          </div>
+          <label class="pj-done"><input type="checkbox" data-project="linux-automation"> Completed</label>
+        </div>
+        <div class="pj-body">
+          <details>
+            <summary>What you'll learn</summary>
+            <div class="pj-section"><ul>
+              <li>Writing safe Bash: <code>set -euo pipefail</code>, functions, exit codes and arguments</li>
+              <li>Reading system state with <code>df</code>, <code>free</code>, <code>systemctl</code> and <code>journalctl</code></li>
+              <li>Scheduling with cron <em>and</em> systemd timers, and understanding the difference</li>
+              <li>Key-based SSH and copying backups to a second machine with <code>rsync</code></li>
+            </ul></div>
+          </details>
+          <details>
+            <summary>Steps</summary>
+            <div class="pj-section"><ol>
+              <li><strong>Get a Linux box.</strong> Use a local VM (Multipass, VirtualBox or WSL2) or a free-tier cloud instance.</li>
+              <li><strong>Write <code>healthcheck.sh</code>.</strong> Warn when disk usage is above 80% or free memory is below 10%, and when a named service (e.g. <code>nginx</code>) is not active. Exit non-zero on any failure.</li>
+              <li><strong>Write <code>backup.sh</code>.</strong> Tar and gzip a directory with a timestamp, keep the last 7 archives and delete older ones.</li>
+              <li><strong>Schedule both.</strong> Run the health check every 5 minutes with cron, and the backup nightly with a systemd timer.</li>
+              <li><strong>Ship backups off-box.</strong> Set up SSH keys and <code>rsync</code> the archive to a second VM or an S3 bucket.</li>
+              <li><strong>Lint.</strong> Run <code>shellcheck</code> on every script and fix all warnings.</li>
+            </ol>
+            <pre><code>#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+
+THRESHOLD=${THRESHOLD:-80}
+status=0
+
+while read -r use mount; do
+  pct=${use%\%}
+  if (( pct &gt; THRESHOLD )); then
+    echo "WARN: $mount is ${pct}% full"
+    status=1
+  fi
+done &lt; &lt;(df -h --output=pcent,target -x tmpfs -x devtmpfs | tail -n +2)
+
+for svc in "$@"; do
+  systemctl is-active --quiet "$svc" || { echo "FAIL: $svc is not running"; status=1; }
+done
+
+exit "$status"</code></pre></div>
+          </details>
+          <details>
+            <summary>Done when</summary>
+            <div class="pj-section"><ul>
+              <li><code>shellcheck *.sh</code> reports nothing</li>
+              <li>Stopping the service makes the health check exit with code 1</li>
+              <li><code>systemctl list-timers</code> shows your backup timer, and only 7 archives exist after a week</li>
+            </ul></div>
+          </details>
+          <details>
+            <summary>Stretch goals &amp; résumé bullet</summary>
+            <div class="pj-section">
+              <ul>
+                <li>Send failures to a Slack or Discord webhook with <code>curl</code></li>
+                <li>Package the scripts as an Ansible role so you can deploy them to any server</li>
+              </ul>
+              <p style="margin-top:0.9rem;" class="pj-resume">"Automated server health monitoring and 7-day rotating backups with Bash, cron and systemd timers, with off-host replication over SSH."</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+        </div>
+      </article>
+
+      <!-- ── 2 ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
+      <article class="pj-card" id="containerise-app" data-level="beginner">
+        <div class="pj-head">
+          <div class="pj-num">02</div>
+          <div>
+            <h2>Containerise a 3-Tier App with Docker Compose</h2>
+            <p>Package a web frontend, an API and a PostgreSQL database into containers and run the whole stack with one command.</p>
+            <div class="pj-meta">
+              <span class="pj-pill lvl-beginner">Beginner</span>
+              <span class="pj-pill">~1 weekend</span>
+              <span class="pj-pill">Docker</span><span class="pj-pill">Compose</span><span class="pj-pill">PostgreSQL</span><span class="pj-pill">Nginx</span>
+            </div>
+          </div>
+          <label class="pj-done"><input type="checkbox" data-project="containerise-app"> Completed</label>
+        </div>
+        <div class="pj-body">
+          <details>
+            <summary>Architecture</summary>
+            <div class="pj-section">
+              <div class="pj-arch">browser → nginx (frontend, :80) → api (:8000) → postgres (:5432, named volume)</div>
+              <p>Use any small API you like (Flask, FastAPI, Express or Go). A to-do list with create, list and delete endpoints is enough.</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+          <details>
+            <summary>Steps</summary>
+            <div class="pj-section"><ol>
+              <li><strong>Write a multi-stage Dockerfile</strong> for the API, so the final image has no compilers or dev dependencies.</li>
+              <li><strong>Run as non-root</strong> and add a <code>HEALTHCHECK</code>.</li>
+              <li><strong>Serve the frontend</strong> from an <code>nginx:alpine</code> image that proxies <code>/api</code> to the API container.</li>
+              <li><strong>Write <code>compose.yaml</code></strong> with a named volume for Postgres, a <code>.env</code> file for secrets and <code>depends_on</code> with <code>condition: service_healthy</code>.</li>
+              <li><strong>Measure.</strong> Compare image sizes before and after multi-stage builds and record the numbers in your README.</li>
+            </ol>
+            <pre><code>services:
+  db:
+    image: postgres:16-alpine
+    environment:
+      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD}
+    volumes: [pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data]
+    healthcheck:
+      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U postgres"]
+      interval: 5s
+      retries: 5
+  api:
+    build: ./api
+    environment:
+      DATABASE_URL: postgres://postgres:${DB_PASSWORD}@db:5432/postgres
+    depends_on:
+      db: { condition: service_healthy }
+  web:
+    build: ./web
+    ports: ["8080:80"]
+    depends_on: [api]
+volumes:
+  pgdata:</code></pre></div>
+          </details>
