+              <span class="pj-pill lvl-intermediate">Intermediate</span>
+              <span class="pj-pill">~1–2 weeks</span>
+              <span class="pj-pill">Kubernetes</span><span class="pj-pill">kind</span><span class="pj-pill">Helm</span><span class="pj-pill">Ingress</span><span class="pj-pill">HPA</span>
+            </div>
+          </div>
+          <label class="pj-done"><input type="checkbox" data-project="k8s-helm"> Completed</label>
+        </div>
+        <div class="pj-body">
+          <details>
+            <summary>Steps</summary>
+            <div class="pj-section"><ol>
+              <li><strong>Create a cluster</strong> with <code>kind</code> (3 nodes) and install the ingress-nginx controller and metrics-server.</li>
+              <li><strong>Write raw manifests first:</strong> a Deployment and Service for the API and web, a StatefulSet and PVC for Postgres, and a Secret for the DB password.</li>
+              <li><strong>Add probes</strong> (readiness and liveness) and <strong>resource requests and limits</strong> to every container.</li>
+              <li><strong>Convert to a Helm chart</strong> with <code>helm create</code>, then move image tags, replicas and hostnames into <code>values.yaml</code>.</li>
+              <li><strong>Add an HPA</strong> on the API (CPU 70%), load-test with <code>hey</code> or <code>k6</code>, and watch it scale.</li>
+              <li><strong>Practise rollouts:</strong> deploy a broken image, watch the readiness probe stop it, then run <code>helm rollback</code>.</li>
+            </ol>
+            <pre><code>kind create cluster --name lab --config kind.yaml
+helm upgrade --install ingress-nginx ingress-nginx \
+  --repo https://kubernetes.github.io/ingress-nginx -n ingress-nginx --create-namespace
+helm upgrade --install app ./chart -n app --create-namespace \
+  --set api.image.tag=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)
+kubectl -n app get pods,svc,ingress,hpa
+kubectl -n app rollout status deploy/app-api</code></pre></div>
