From e67ee85a264f35ed5be1d45284820e34bfb4b9f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:51:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] Give every blog article its own page, plus an RSS feed

Articles used to live inside one JS object in blog.html and opened in a
modal, so search engines and share links only ever saw blog.html.

- Article sources move to _blog/posts/*.html with metadata in posts.json
- _blog/build.mjs generates blog-<slug>.html pages (TechArticle and
  breadcrumb JSON-LD, TOC, honest reading time, copy buttons, share
  links, previous/next and related articles), refreshes the blog index,
  sitemap and search index, and writes feed.xml
- Fix article code: restore lost line continuations in Helm commands,
  correct PromQL aggregation, read Grafana's generated password, look up
  the AMI instead of hardcoding it, replace deprecated npm/compose/
  semgrep usage and pin trivy-action
- Replace the newsletter form, which discarded emails, with RSS and
  LinkedIn follow links

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016Le4ebuVBvTqc4a3Q8F1Aj
---
