-docker run -d -p 3000:3000 --name myapp myapp:1.0
-
-# List running containers
-docker ps
-
-# View container logs
-docker logs myapp -f
-
-# Stop and remove container
-docker stop myapp && docker rm myapp
-
-# List images
-docker images
-
-# Remove unused resources
-docker system prune</code></pre>
-
-      <h2>Multi-Stage Builds (Production Best Practice)</h2>
-      <p>Multi-stage builds let you use a large build image (with compilers and dev tools) but produce a tiny final image with only what's needed to run:</p>
-
-      <pre><code># Stage 1: Build
-FROM golang:1.21 AS builder
-WORKDIR /app
-COPY . .
-RUN go build -o myapp .
-
-# Stage 2: Run (tiny final image)
-FROM alpine:3.19
-COPY --from=builder /app/myapp /myapp
-CMD ["/myapp"]</code></pre>
-
-      <div class="article-callout">
-        <p><strong>Result:</strong> The Go build image is ~800MB. The final Alpine image is ~10MB. Multi-stage builds are essential for production.</p>
-      </div>
-
-      <h2>Docker Compose</h2>
-      <p>For applications with multiple services (app + database + cache), use Docker Compose:</p>
-
-      <pre><code>version: '3.9'
-services:
-  app:
-    build: .
-    ports:
-      - "3000:3000"
-    environment:
-      DATABASE_URL: postgres://user:pass@db:5432/mydb
-    depends_on:
-      - db
-      - redis
-
-  db:
-    image: postgres:16-alpine
-    environment:
-      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: pass
-      POSTGRES_USER: user
-      POSTGRES_DB: mydb
-    volumes:
-      - pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data
-
-  redis:
-    image: redis:7-alpine
-
-volumes:
-  pgdata:</code></pre>
-
-      <p>Run everything with a single command: <code>docker compose up -d</code></p>
-
-      <h2>Next Steps</h2>
-      <ul>
-        <li>Learn Kubernetes to orchestrate containers at scale</li>
-        <li>Set up a private Docker registry (ECR, GCR, or Docker Hub)</li>
-        <li>Add Docker to your CI/CD pipeline with GitHub Actions</li>
-        <li>Explore container security scanning with Trivy</li>
-      </ul>
