-  'cicd-github-actions': {
-    title: 'Build a CI/CD Pipeline with GitHub Actions from Scratch',
-    meta: '🔁 CI/CD · Feb 3, 2026 · 10 min read · Beginner',
-    body: `
-      <h1>Build a CI/CD Pipeline with GitHub Actions from Scratch</h1>
-      <div class="blog-meta" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
-        <span class="blog-meta-item">🔁 CI/CD</span>
-        <span class="blog-meta-item">📅 Feb 3, 2026</span>
-        <span class="blog-meta-item">⏱ 10 min read</span>
-      </div>
-
-      <p>GitHub Actions is one of the most powerful and beginner-friendly CI/CD tools available today. It's built directly into GitHub — no external servers, no plugins to manage. In this guide, you'll build a complete pipeline from scratch.</p>
-
-      <h2>How GitHub Actions Works</h2>
-      <p>Workflows are defined in YAML files inside <code>.github/workflows/</code> in your repository. They are triggered by events — pushes, pull requests, schedules, and more.</p>
-
-      <h2>Your First Workflow</h2>
-      <pre><code># .github/workflows/ci.yml
-name: CI Pipeline
-
-on:
-  push:
-    branches: [main, develop]
-  pull_request:
-    branches: [main]
-
-jobs:
-  test:
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    steps:
-      - name: Checkout code
-        uses: actions/checkout@v4
-
-      - name: Setup Node.js
-        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
-        with:
-          node-version: '20'
-          cache: 'npm'
-
-      - name: Install dependencies
-        run: npm ci
-
-      - name: Run tests
-        run: npm test
-
-      - name: Build
-        run: npm run build</code></pre>
-
-      <h2>Adding Docker Build & Push</h2>
-      <pre><code>  docker:
-    needs: test
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
-    steps:
-      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
-
-      - name: Login to Docker Hub
-        uses: docker/login-action@v3
-        with:
-          username: \${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}
-          password: \${{ secrets.DOCKER_TOKEN }}
-
-      - name: Build and push
-        uses: docker/build-push-action@v5
-        with:
-          push: true
-          tags: myuser/myapp:\${{ github.sha }}</code></pre>
-
-      <div class="article-callout">
-        <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Never hardcode credentials. Add secrets in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions.</p>
-      </div>
-
-      <h2>Key GitHub Actions Concepts</h2>
-      <ul>
-        <li><strong>Workflow</strong> — the YAML file defining your automation</li>
-        <li><strong>Job</strong> — a set of steps that run on the same runner</li>
-        <li><strong>Step</strong> — a single task (run a command or use an action)</li>
-        <li><strong>Action</strong> — reusable unit from the Actions Marketplace</li>
-        <li><strong>Runner</strong> — the machine that executes your workflow</li>
-        <li><strong>Secrets</strong> — encrypted variables for credentials</li>
-      </ul>
-    `
-  },
