+<h2 id="speed-it-up-caching-and-parallel-jobs">Speed it up: caching and parallel jobs</h2>
+<p>Jobs run in parallel unless you link them with <code>needs:</code>. A <strong>matrix</strong> runs the same job across versions or platforms:</p>
+<pre><code>jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    strategy:
+      matrix:
+        node: [20, 22]
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+        with:
+          node-version: ${{ matrix.node }}
+          cache: npm          # caches ~/.npm keyed on package-lock.json
+      - run: npm ci
+      - run: npm test</code></pre>
+<p>Docker builds can reuse layers between runs through the GitHub Actions cache:</p>
+<pre><code>      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3
+      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v6
+        with:
+          push: true
+          tags: ghcr.io/you/app:${{ github.sha }}
+          cache-from: type=gha
+          cache-to: type=gha,mode=max</code></pre>
+
+<h2 id="least-privilege-permissions">Least-privilege permissions</h2>
+<p>Every workflow gets a <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code>. Restrict it to what the workflow needs:</p>
+<pre><code>permissions:
+  contents: read
+  packages: write      # only if pushing to GHCR
+  id-token: write      # only if using OIDC to a cloud</code></pre>
+
+<h2 id="deploy-to-the-cloud-without-stored-keys-oidc">Deploy to the cloud without stored keys (OIDC)</h2>
+<p>Instead of saving AWS access keys as secrets, let GitHub issue a short-lived token that AWS trusts:</p>
+<pre><code>  deploy:
+    needs: docker
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    environment: production         # can require manual approval
+    permissions:
+      id-token: write
+      contents: read
+    steps:
+      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4
+        with:
+          role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/github-deploy
+          aws-region: eu-west-1
+      - run: aws sts get-caller-identity</code></pre>
+<p>In AWS, create an IAM OIDC provider for <code>token.actions.githubusercontent.com</code>, and a role whose trust policy only allows <code>repo:you/app:environment:production</code>.</p>
+
+<h2 id="environments-and-approvals">Environments and approvals</h2>
+<p>GitHub <strong>Environments</strong> (Settings → Environments) add required reviewers, wait timers, branch restrictions and environment-specific secrets. A job with <code>environment: production</code> pauses until someone approves it, which gives you continuous delivery with a human gate.</p>
+
+<h2 id="reusable-workflows">Reusable workflows</h2>
+<p>When several repos share the same pipeline, define it once:</p>
+<pre><code># .github/workflows/build.yml in a shared repo
+on:
+  workflow_call:
+    inputs:
+      image: { type: string, required: true }
+
+# caller repo
+jobs:
+  build:
+    uses: your-org/ci-templates/.github/workflows/build.yml@v1
+    with:
+      image: ghcr.io/your-org/api</code></pre>
